    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d796">

                <pb facs="0897" n="1731" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1731"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 837.711/10</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Cuba</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Gonzales</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-02-16T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 16, 1918, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Major Van Natta and Captain Robert Goelet, U. S. A[rmy], have been designated as
                    representatives of the United States Censorship Board to act as liaison
                    officers, in Cuba. They will arrive about the 15th instant.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
